Description: elanmoc: skip the re-enroll check entirely on 0c77
 elanmoc-skip-reenroll-check-when-empty.patch skips MOC_ENROLL_REENROLL_CHECK
 (40 ff 22) only when nothing is enrolled yet, on the assumption that the
 command is merely pointless in that case. On this FW the command is not
 implemented at all: with one finger already enrolled it is sent for real,
 the read times out and the enroll fails with enroll-unknown-error. That
 made it impossible to enroll a second finger. Skip it for
 ELANMOC_PROTO_V2 regardless of the enrolled count.
Author: local
Last-Update: 2026-07-30
Index: libfprint-1.95.1+tod1/libfprint/drivers/elanmoc/elanmoc.c
===================================================================
--- libfprint-1.95.1+tod1.orig/libfprint/drivers/elanmoc/elanmoc.c
+++ libfprint-1.95.1+tod1/libfprint/drivers/elanmoc/elanmoc.c
@@ -484,7 +484,12 @@ elan_enroll_run_state (FpiSsm *ssm, FpDe
       break;
 
     case MOC_ENROLL_REENROLL_CHECK:
-      if (self->curr_enrolled == 0)
+      /* This FW does not implement the re-enroll check (40 ff 22) at all, not
+       * just when the storage is empty: with a finger already enrolled the
+       * command is sent for real and the read times out, so enrolling a
+       * second finger could never succeed.
+       */
+      if (self->curr_enrolled == 0 || elanmoc_is_proto_v2 (dev))
         {
           self->num_frames = 0;
           fpi_ssm_next_state (ssm);
